---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="Website Terms" description="Terms of use for the Oakheart Technologies website, including prices, examples and results, links, and limits of liability.">
  <article class="wrap section">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl">Website Terms</h1>
    <p class="ph mt-4 inline-block text-sm font-semibold">DRAFT: have this reviewed before launch</p>
    <div class="prose-measure mt-8 space-y-5 [&_h2]:mt-8 [&_h2]:text-2xl">
      <p>Last updated: October 2026</p>
      <p>
        These terms cover your use of this website, which is operated by Oakheart Technologies in Spokane, WA. By using
        the site, you agree to them.
      </p>

      <h2>Use of this site</h2>
      <p>
        The content on this site is provided for general information about Oakheart Technologies and its services. It
        isn’t a contract or an offer. Any work is governed by a separate written agreement or quote.
      </p>

      <h2>Prices and quotes</h2>
      <p>
        Prices shown are starting prices and may change. The price for any work is the one confirmed in writing before
        the work begins. Prices exclude any applicable sales tax, which varies by state.
      </p>

      <h2>Examples and results</h2>
      <p>
        Case studies and figures on this site describe specific past situations. They show what was done in those cases,
        not what will happen in yours. Results depend on your business, your systems and your circumstances, and nothing
        here is a guarantee.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The site’s text, design and logos belong to Oakheart Technologies unless noted. Please don’t copy them without
        permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Other companies’ names</h2>
      <p>
        Names of other companies and products mentioned on this site, such as Microsoft, QuickBooks, Asana, Unity and
        Meta Quest, belong to their owners. Mentioning them doesn’t mean they sponsor or endorse Oakheart.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        The site links to other websites. I don’t control them and I’m not responsible for their content or practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Please use the site and its contact form for genuine inquiries. Don’t use them to send spam, to attempt to disrupt
        or break into the site, or to collect its content automatically.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided as is. I make reasonable efforts to keep it accurate and available but don’t guarantee it.
      </p>

      <h2>Limit of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent the law allows, Oakheart Technologies isn’t liable for any loss or damage that comes from
        using this website or relying on its content. Work done for clients is covered by its own written agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Washington.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>I may update these terms. The date at the top shows when they last changed.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions: <a class="text-royal underline" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
